Test Branch 0.3.4-test 2026-07-24

Design

- Improved the trade deals offered by non-player factions
- Added more detailed agendas for non-player factions (e.g. based on clans, norms, etc) to make their diplomacy actions more consistent 
- Non-player factions can now issue Requests for a specific item to be delivered within a certain number of turns. If fulfilled, it gives +10 Opinion and triggers a reward event.
- New relationship state, Trade Embargo, during which the 2 factions can't trade or issue Requests. Triggered after each battle, lasting 5 turns.
- Trade no longer has a minimum Opinion requirement
- New relationship state, Non-Aggression Pact, during which the 2 factions can't attack each other. Triggered by 'Declare Friendship' and 'Declare Alliance' diplomacy actions.

- Alliances:
  - New relationship state, Alliance, Triggered by 'Declare Alliance' diplomacy action
  - Requires 20+ Opinion and both sides having less than 2 ongoing alliances
  - Comes with an unlimited Non-Aggression Pact and Right of Passage
  - Triggers an alliance event with a long-term bonus
  - Causes an Alliance Cooldown for 10 turns, during which the alliance can't be broken
  - Broken by new 'Break Alliance' diplomacy action, which applies a long-term Opinion malus
  - Added Opinion malus for attacking another faction's allies
  - New tribe state, Coalition Leader, which requires being allied to 2 factions with fewer Victory Points, and gives +50% Culture/turn to the Coalition Leader

- Too Much Debt no longer impacts Happiness/turn, instead it now blocks issuing of Requests and most diplomacy actions 
- Debt tolerances at each opinion level are doubled (Angry: 5 -> 10, Upset: 25 -> 50, Cautious: 50 -> 100, Friendly:100 -> 200)
- 'Right of Passage' diplomacy action reworked into 'Temporary Passage' and only offers right of passage for 2 turns
- Added Opinion malus based on number of Spiritual Sites in which both tribes have invested Worship Points
- Traders Clan now gives +0.5 Happiness per owned item type, decreased from +1

- Band Culture/turn and Science/turn now have their baselines broken down into 0.1/adult (age 15+) and 0.05/child (age 5-14) instead of +0.1/person of any age. This makes high fertility take longer to pay off, and slows down overall pace of progression.
- Higher risk outcome in hunting events now gives +30 Food, increased from +20

UI

- Improved structure and visuals of Diplomacy menu
- Added separate menu showing all relationships between all factions (accessible via new button in top-right toolbar)
- Improved faction relationship summary tooltips
- Made clan synergy effect tooltips easier to access in clans menu

Bugs Fixed

- Fixed issue where new diplomatic agreements sometimes didn't cancel existing intentions to attack or trade

Known Issues

- Sometimes number of assignable fighters shows a negative number in the numerator
- Sometimes an empty acknowledgement appears without text
- Sometimes prey cluster 'hunt' action isn't available when it should be (its button remains grayed out). Haven't been able to recreate the issue, please reach out if you encounter it
- Linux: game sometimes gets stuck during autosave (seems to be due to dual-boot setup with storing game files on external NTFS drive; works fine when files are moved to EXT4 drive)
